  "workItemId": "ATM-GOV-0306",
  "title": "Mutation adapter, lineage, and equivalence governance",
  "status": "done",
  "milestone": "ATM-GOV-PLAN4-R1",
  "dependencies": [
    "ATM-GOV-0285"
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "ACC-1: a pinned deterministic mutation adapter (StrykerJS or an in-process fixture adapter) executes only inside an ATM-GOV-0285-selected probe window.",
    "ACC-2: every observation writes a replayable lineage record with mutant id, killed/survived outcome, lower/upper score bounds, and seed/digest identity.",
    "ACC-3: equivalence governance classifies survivors as equivalent or non-equivalent; raw tool pass never directly authorizes close.",
    "ACC-4: unsupported or inconclusive adapter results fail closed and must not return pass.",
    "ACC-5: lineage outputs are consumable by ATM-GOV-0293 as survivor/equivalence evidence that may strengthen or weaken confidence, but must not be the sole matching authority.",
    "ACC-6: focused tests cover killed, survived, equivalent, unsupported, and replay-from-digest paths."
  ],
